# scitex-cards environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and edit values for your setup.
# CLI flags always override env vars when both are given. Variables follow
# the SciTeX ecosystem convention: SCITEX_<MODULE>_<NAME>.
#
# THIS FILE DESCRIBED A STORE THAT NO LONGER EXISTS until 2026-08-16. It
# documented a `..._TASKS` variable pointing at a `tasks.yaml`, and a
# user-global/project-local pair of YAML directories to fall back through.
# None of that is how the store is chosen any more: there is ONE axis,
# `$SCITEX_CARDS_DB`, holding a PostgreSQL URL, and there
# has been no zero-config default since 2026-08-13 — an unset target REFUSES
# rather than inventing a file. A copied-and-edited `.env` following the old
# text would have set a variable nothing reads, which is worse than setting
# nothing: it looks configured.

# The canonical store: a PostgreSQL URL. Nothing else is accepted — a
# filesystem path is REFUSED at the door rather than opened, because the
# retired file engine is gone and coercing a path only ever manufactured a
# second, empty store that answered every query.
# There is no tier below the config file — leave this unset only if
# `.scitex/cards/config.json` names a `store.target`.
# SCITEX_CARDS_DB=postgresql://scitex_cards@127.0.0.1:55432/scitex_cards

# Who this process writes as. Stamped onto every card and used to resolve
# `scope=agent:<id>`. Agents get this from their sac spec, not from here.
# SCITEX_CARDS_AGENT_ID=your-agent-id

# Default scope filter for `list-tasks` when none is passed.
# SCITEX_CARDS_SCOPE=agent:your-agent-id

# Run `scitex-cards resolve-store` to print what a process actually
# resolved, and which tier supplied it.
